    {
      "id": "9ntdnr1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Prehistoric Period of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s6x208z",
      "content": "The prehistoric period refers to the time before the invention of writing. It is known mainly through tools, cave paintings, and fossils."
    },
    {
      "id": "2h1225c",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Period</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Features</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Important Sites</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Paleolithic Age (Old Stone Age)</p>",
            "<p>Use of crude stone tools, hunting and food gathering</p>",
            "<p>Bhimbetka, Hunsgi</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mesolithic Age (Middle Stone Age)</p>",
            "<p>Microlith tools, beginning of domestication</p>",
            "<p>Bagor, Adamgarh</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Neolithic Age (New Stone Age)</p>",
            "<p>Polished stone tools, agriculture begins</p>",
            "<p>Mehrgarh, Burzahom</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fvpg0fo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Indus Valley Civilization (Harappan Civilization)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w40vp4b",
      "content": "Time Period: Approximately 2500 BCE – 1750 BCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ly6rg2z",
      "content": "The Indus Valley Civilization was one of the world's earliest urban civilizations. It developed mainly along the Indus River and its tributaries."
    },
    {
      "id": "89aw87j",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Major Features"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nxhi9oc",
      "content": "• Well-planned cities with grid pattern"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "rttv2hz",
      "content": "• Advanced drainage system                                                        "
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "3nd4b7p",
      "content": "• Use of standardized bricks"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ac2ve9m",
      "content": "• Trade with Mesopotamia"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3s0ggzb",
      "content": "• Use of seals and undeciphered script"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "febf3yz",
      "content": "• Absence of large temples or palaces"
    },
    {
      "id": "l8l5e7l",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4.Major Sites and Their Importance"
    },
    {
      "id": "8pcis9t",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Site</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Important Feature</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Harappa</p>",
            "<p>First discovered site (1921)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mohenjo-daro</p>",
            "<p>Great Bath and large granary</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Lothal</p>",
            "<p>Dockyard and maritime trade</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Kalibangan</p>",
            "<p>Evidence of ploughed field</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Dholavira</p>",
            "<p>Advanced water conservation system</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Rakhigarhi</p>",
            "<p>Largest Harappan site in India</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ne63tzt",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.Town Planning"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oewqkhk",
      "content": "• Cities were divided into Citadel and Lower Town"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b2rjc8j",
      "content": "• Houses were made of baked bricks"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mnx6phm",
      "content": "• Roads intersected at right angles"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2vfm6sf",
      "content": "• Covered drainage system was highly advanced"
    },
    {
      "id": "ymwpakr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "6.Economy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gu0vrd3",
      "content": "• Agriculture was the main occupation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lbuo7i9",
      "content": "• Wheat and barley were major crops"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "1912sxf",
      "content": "• Trade existed with Mesopotamia"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2l9btve",
      "content": "• Standard weights and measures were used"
    },
    {
      "id": "qehivnw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "7.Religion"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "pp7yg2i",
      "content": "• Worship of Mother Goddess"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2yau04e",
      "content": "• Pashupati seal suggests proto‑Shiva worship                                                     "
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w1sm6pb",
      "content": "• Sacred animals included bull and unicorn"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "xhrjx5v",
      "content": "• Peepal tree considered sacred"
    },
    {
      "id": "4720m5m",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "8.Decline of the Indus Valley Civilization"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rfcmh5v",
      "content": "• Climate change and drying of rivers"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "hjvejvu",
      "content": "• Floods and natural disasters"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
